# Traylor Pro Commercial Lead Finder — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for local development. NEVER commit real values.
# In Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which data the app uses.
#   demo      fictional demo data stored only in this browser (default; also the fallback)
#   supabase  the dedicated Lead Finder Supabase project, with invite-only email sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_DATA_SOURCE=demo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dedicated Lead Finder Supabase project ONLY (never any other Traylor Pro project).
# Both values are PUBLIC by design: they are built into the page every visitor downloads.
# They are safe to expose ONLY because row-level security protects every table.
#   URL:  Supabase → Project Settings → Data API → Project URL
#   Key:  Supabase → Project Settings → API Keys → the "anon" (legacy) or "publishable" key
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# (or, instead of the anon key:)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT USED BY THIS APP — do not add them anywhere:
#   service_role / secret key, database password, database connection string.
# The app has no server-side secret. If a secret key is put in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable by
# mistake, the app refuses to start (and you should rotate that key in Supabase).
